{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1351803-crime-pays-larceny-stealth-and-ebon-shadow","id":1351803,"title":"Crime Pays: Larceny, Stealth, and Ebon Shadow","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-30T00:24:28-08:00","id":1351803,"title":"Crime Pays: Larceny, Stealth, and Ebon Shadow","content":"I finally have a chance to play instead of ST and I'm thinking of making a Night Caste Yakuza type character. Larcency, Stealth, Ebon Shadow. Going for that master criminal / assassin build that no one in my group has. <br /> <br /> Has anyone used Ebon Shadow? I know it requires/rewards a high Stealth. What's the best way to make a great assassin out of it? I heard that Snake style combo's well- I think its because Snake can ignore soak and ES can turn 0 soak into a lot of bonus damage. I don't know if Tiger's Stealth side matters that much that it combos with Ebon Shadow, or if Tiger is a a good place to start instead. <br /> <br /> I'm thinking of taking Larceny Supernal even though Stealth has more charms because I like the flavor more. I'm planning to start at Essence 3 though, so it doesn't really matter that much. <br /> <br /> So for the Crime Side of my character, I'm thinking Larceny and Stealth. That gives me a lot of Out Of Combat Utility (both mechanically and RP wise).<br /> For the Assassin/Killer side of my character, I'm thinking Ebon Shadow with a splash of Snake (just to get Armor Penetrating Fang Strike), and Dodge to keep me alive. <br /> <br /> So that's where I am: Larceny, Stealth, Ebon Shadow, Dodge and a splash of Snake. <br /> <br /> Any build advice? Useful artifacts? Good Charms to add in other skills? good synergy? etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T03:34:06-08:00","id":1351827,"title":"","content":"&quot;Are you a lone wolf or part of an organization&quot; is the first question that needs to be asked. If part of an organization are you now the leader or still an operative and are you planning on changing that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800080\">I express my opinions, but YSMV; Your Stories May Vary.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Formerly known as wyrmpuff</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12288-mal-akh","name":"Mal'akh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12288_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T08:04:45-08:00","id":1351865,"title":"","content":"Athletics and Stealth.<br /> <br /> <br /> Blinding Battle Feint to start combat in Stealth. Foe Vaulting Method to force Unexpected Attacks. Thunderbolt Attack Prana. Athletics Excellency for Rushes. Guardian Fog Approach is very useful.<br /> <br /> Dodge is good. Larceny is good.<br /> <br /> Snake is good. But Armor Penatrating Fang Strike is pretty deep and it doesn't share a Form Weapon. Seven Points of Weakness already ignores 10 points of Armored Soak -- I don't think Snake is worth it.<br /> <br /> Tiger, on the other hand, adds damage, syngergizes with Stealth and shares Tiger Claws.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T16:07:35-08:00","id":1351927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mal'akh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1351803-crime-pays-larceny-stealth-and-ebon-shadow?p=1351827#post1351827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Are you a lone wolf or part of an organization&quot; is the first question that needs to be asked. If part of an organization are you now the leader or still an operative and are you planning on changing that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Great question. The game is set in the Western Ocean and island hops. Everywhere from the Blessed Isle to Fajad to Blue Haven, An Teng, and next is Caul. I don't think I want to be part of a Creation-Spanning crime ring. I see my Yakuza as a man who became more than mortal but doesn't want to become an Oyabun, a boss. He doesn't want to order people arounda nd keep up a public face. He <i>likes</i> being a thug. Now he's a Super One. He'll bring his talents to the pirate armada the other Solars have. Lone Wolf. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1351803-crime-pays-larceny-stealth-and-ebon-shadow?p=1351865#post1351865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Athletics and Stealth.<br /> <br /> <br /> Blinding Battle Feint to start combat in Stealth. Foe Vaulting Method to force Unexpected Attacks. Thunderbolt Attack Prana. Athletics Excellency for Rushes. Guardian Fog Approach is very useful.<br /> <br /> Dodge is good. Larceny is good.<br /> <br /> Snake is good. But Armor Penatrating Fang Strike is pretty deep and it doesn't share a Form Weapon. Seven Points of Weakness already ignores 10 points of Armored Soak -- I don't think Snake is worth it.<br /> <br /> Tiger, on the other hand, adds damage, syngergizes with Stealth and shares Tiger Claws.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Great advice, thank you. I'll drop Snake for Tiger. Any specific ability I should rush for? Best Claw or Knife artifact? We're pretty loose with form weapons so I might just throw in an evocation that lets it count for both MAs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T17:14:30-08:00","id":1351935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> He'll bring his talents to the pirate armada the other Solars have. Lone Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then Martial Arts, Dodge, Athletics, Larceny and Stealth are your bread and butter skills with other skills to round out your character depending on what else you want your character to be. I highly suggest Medicine since I used that to good effect whenever I played a character with Ebon Shadow Style.We are talking about hitting vital points after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800080\">I express my opinions, but YSMV; Your Stories May Vary.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Formerly known as wyrmpuff</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12288-mal-akh","name":"Mal'akh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12288_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T17:28:11-08:00","id":1351938,"title":"","content":"I thought about adding Medicine for flavor but our team Zenith already has it. I'm trying to avoid anyone else's niche. <br /> <br /> Eclipse: Sail, War (pirate army), SPSitV, Grapple Brawl<br /> Twilight: ISoB, Melee, Survival, Rank 3 Familiar<br /> Twilight: Bureaucracy, Thrown, Occult, Socialize<br /> Zenith: Presence, Max Rank Ally: Young DB<br /> <br /> The Eclipse is taking over ST so I was considering going with Strike!Brawl and Resistance but I think we have enough to do in combat and out Out of Combat is a little lacking (in practice, a LOT lacking)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T05:35:37-08:00","id":1351997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1351803-crime-pays-larceny-stealth-and-ebon-shadow?p=1351927#post1351927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Great question. The game is set in the Western Ocean and island hops. Everywhere from the Blessed Isle to Fajad to Blue Haven, An Teng, and next is Caul. I don't think I want to be part of a Creation-Spanning crime ring. I see my Yakuza as a man who became more than mortal but doesn't want to become an Oyabun, a boss. He doesn't want to order people arounda nd keep up a public face. He <i>likes</i> being a thug. Now he's a Super One. He'll bring his talents to the pirate armada the other Solars have. Lone Wolf. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Great advice, thank you. I'll drop Snake for Tiger. Any specific ability I should rush for? Best Claw or Knife artifact? We're pretty loose with form weapons so I might just throw in an evocation that lets it count for both MAs.</div> </div> </div> </div>My assumption is that you like Ebon Shadow and Stealth and will be investing heavily in these Abilities. I presume also that you're going to invest in Athletics and Dodge.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Crimson Leaping Cat Technique 7/10<br /> You will want to Rush to get into range with your attacks. Extra Initiative is a nice benefit, extra dice on attacks is what makes this worth 4m. Pretty situational though. Not really worth &quot;rushing&quot;<br /> <br /> Striking Cat Fury Claws 9/10<br /> Probably the only Charm I'd start with. Bonus Withering damage is great. It's costly, and you're unlikely to get the benefit against fleeing opponents (if the ST is softballing you, you don't need the benefit; if the enemy is good at Disengaging you won't get your attack). But it's a nice chunk of <i>post soak</i> damage.<br /> <br /> Tiger Form 5/10<br /> I love Tiger Form. But you're only going to use it after launching a Decisive when mopping up or when fighting a Smasher.<br /> <br /> Celestial Tiger Hide 9/10<br /> Ebon Shadow is incompatible with armor. This is amazing.<br /> <br /> Iron Claw Grip 5/10<br /> If you pick up Wood Dragon's Claw and branch out into Black Claw, this becomes a 10/10 Charm. But Ebon Shadow isn't really a &quot;grapple&quot; MA unless you're using a fighting chain... which you won't be.<br /> <br /> Prey Maiming Frenzy 5/10<br /> As above. It's a good Charm. It doesn't synergize.<br /> <br /> Raging Tiger Pounce - 8/10<br /> Undodgable is a brilliant buff, especially as your Charms are so expensive. Note it's &quot;pay&quot; Initiative, not &quot;lose&quot;, so Crashed foes can't rise (stuck at -1 Parry, -3 attack, -2 Evasion).<br /> <br /> Spine Shattering Bite - 9.5/10<br /> This is a great Charm that's amazing for a brutal thug.<br /> <br /> Stalking Cat Movement Meditation - 10/10<br /> You are going to be making a lot of surprise attacks and Rushing from Stealth is amazing for you. Grab Shadow Stepping Motion <i>first</i> then rush this. This is the best Charm in Tiger style for you.<br /> <br /> Leap From Cloaking Shadows - 9/10<br /> You're unlikely to get more than three 8s and three 9s on your Decisives, so this is basically double 8s on Decisives with +5(ish) raw damage. That's insane.<br /> <br /> Angry Predator Frenzy 5/10<br /> Again, a great Charm. Again, you'll be in Ebon Shadow Form.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Tl:dr<br /> <br /> Stalking Cat Movement Meditation is the thing to rush. Like Armor Penatrating Fang, it's 4 Charms in and Essence 2.<br /> <br /> If you're willing to house-rule form weapons, then Snake is probably just as good as Tiger. Serpentine Evasion is nice and cheap. Striking Cobra Technique is brilliant. You won't be using Snake Form. And Armor Penatrating Fang is great (plus there's a Reflexive Clash Charm to be had in Snake).<br /> <br /> I'd be considering weapons. Assuming you're not house-ruling form weapons:<br /> <br /> 3) Wood Dragon's Claw 7/10<br /> Pros: Artifact light weapon. Your choice of tags. Very cool. <br /> Cons: Needs to be summoned can be disrupted<br /> <br /> 2) Frost Thorn Knuckles 9.5/10<br /> Pros: Attack from range, bonus Soak and reduced wound penalties (Pain Tolerance is your friend), knock foes Prone for a amazing syngergy with Tiger Style.<br /> Cons: Locks you out of Silken Armor and the like, bonuses for a terrain type your game is unlikely to see.<br /> <br /> 1) Vengeant 10/10<br /> Pros: Be an Iselsi. Have Overwhelming 4 on a light weapon. Concealable. Most powers syngerize with Stealth.<br /> Cons: What cons?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-01T08:10:01-08:00","id":1352011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1351803-crime-pays-larceny-stealth-and-ebon-shadow?p=1351997#post1351997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Be an Iselsi</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm petty sure that doesn't matter unless you're a Dragonblood. It's still really good anyway, but you only need to make your character really hateful, not from Iselsi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-02T10:58:01-08:00","id":1352183,"title":"","content":"As mentioned above, Tiger is probably a better paring than Snake since it has stealth charms and, more importantly, shares tiger claws as a form weapon. Centipede Style also uses tiger claws, and while it doesn't have any stealth charms it's a good general use style and has some nasty multi-attacks and grappling tricks. Falcon Style uses claws and can let you be the Batman by dropping on people from the rafters and ruining their day. Water Dragon Style also uses claws; while it doesn't have any particular synergy Flow Reversal Strike is really nasty if landed from ambush and it might be worth picking up eventually just for the Essence 4 and 5 charms.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, Ebon Shadow also uses knives, which is shared as a form weapon by Swaying Grass Dance Style, which also has some stealth-related tricks. Good choice if you also have Performance.<br /> <br /> That's about it for the breakdown of compatible martial arts. In practice, I'd advise strongly against taking more than 3 different styles since diminishing returns really starts to kick in, unless being a master of many styles is your character's thing in which case go nuts. Now for a little bit of self promotion, if you're looking for artifact Razor Claws with stealth-related Evocations, might I point you towards the homebrew in my signature?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T08:50:18-08:00","id":1352611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1351803-crime-pays-larceny-stealth-and-ebon-shadow#post1351803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> and Dodge to keep me alive.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's your throught process for going for Dodge as opposed to parrying with Martial Arts and using Resistance as a back-up defense?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1351803-crime-pays-larceny-stealth-and-ebon-shadow?p=1351997#post1351997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Frost Thorn Knuckles 9.5/10<br /> Pros: Attack from range, bonus Soak and reduced wound penalties (Pain Tolerance is your friend), knock foes Prone for a amazing syngergy with Tiger Style.<br /> Cons: Locks you out of Silken Armor and the like, bonuses for a terrain type your game is unlikely to see.<br /> <br /> 1) Vengeant 10/10<br /> Pros: Be an Iselsi. Have Overwhelming 4 on a light weapon. Concealable. Most powers syngerize with Stealth.<br /> Cons: What cons?</div> </div> </div> </div>Where can you find Vengeant?<br /> EDIT: Found the Frost Thorn Knuckles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24362,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24362-fredo","user":"Fredo","date":". 12-04-2019, 01:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24362-fredo","name":"Fredo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T08:56:21-08:00","id":1352613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fredo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1351803-crime-pays-larceny-stealth-and-ebon-shadow?p=1352611#post1352611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where can you find Frost Thorn Knuckles and Vengeant?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bArms of the Chosen for the Knuckles. Vengeant is in the Artifacts chapter of the Dragon-Blooded book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T10:47:17-08:00","id":1352642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1351803-crime-pays-larceny-stealth-and-ebon-shadow?p=1352613#post1352613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Arms of the Chosen for the Knuckles. Vengeant is in the Artifacts chapter of the Dragon-Blooded book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you much.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24362-fredo","name":"Fredo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-04T18:45:58-08:00","id":1352721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fredo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1351803-crime-pays-larceny-stealth-and-ebon-shadow?p=1352611#post1352611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's your throught process for going for Dodge as opposed to parrying with Martial Arts and using Resistance as a back-up defense?</div> </div> </div> </div>You broke my heart's grace, fredo! You broke my heart! <br /> <br /> Ok, that aside,<br /> <br /> I haven't done a side by side comparison or anything, but I was planning originally on him being an Ebon Shadow master primarily and using Dodge made me feel more &quot;Ninja-esque&quot;. Stealth, Attack, Dodge, Stealth. Just a theme choice. <br /> <br /> Now that I've actually written the character out, I think I'm leaning harder into the Yakuza Tough Guy side and I might go 50/50 Ebon Shadow and Tiger or just Tiger. In that case I might go for Resistance. <br /> <br /> It has to fit the theme for me. Thats why I'm not taking ISoB and WDC, because there's no way this guy would be a Sorcerer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T06:28:57-08:00","id":1352800,"title":"","content":"Dodge Stealth Ebon Shadow is a good theme.<br /> <br /> Tiger Tough-guy is also good. But Ebon Shadow Night Caste is very strong syngergy, whereas Tiger really lends itself to a straight Dawn (maybe Zenith).<br /> <br /> If you want a lone wolf criminal Night Caste who is still useful to the Circle outside of combat, I'd keep Ebon Shadow.<br /> <br /> Yakuza Tough with Tiger and Resistence is very strong... but what are you doing outside of combat? And in combat what are you doing that isn't done better by a Dawn?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T07:08:57-08:00","id":1352806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1351803-crime-pays-larceny-stealth-and-ebon-shadow?p=1352721#post1352721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't done a side by side comparison or anything, but I was planning originally on him being an Ebon Shadow master primarily and using Dodge made me feel more &quot;Ninja-esque&quot;. Stealth, Attack, Dodge, Stealth. Just a theme choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do remember that with Dodge you can get Rumor of Form at Essence 2 which can let you reflexively enter stealth after dodging an attack for as little as 3 motes, which is al huge power spike for that kinda playstyle. Also the biggest disadvantage of Dodge-focused builds, that being armor restriction, is already moot if you take Ebon Shadow since that MA is naked-only.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1311230-badassoverlord-s-assorted-homebrew-folder\" target=\"_blank\">Are you in the market for some Martial Arts? Perhaps some custom Artifacts for your campaign?</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10131-badassoverlord","name":"BadassOverlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10131_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-05T18:44:28-08:00","id":1352934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BadassOverlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1351803-crime-pays-larceny-stealth-and-ebon-shadow?p=1352806#post1352806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do remember that with Dodge you can get Rumor of Form at Essence 2 which can let you reflexively enter stealth after dodging an attack for as little as 3 motes, which is al huge power spike for that kinda playstyle. Also the biggest disadvantage of Dodge-focused builds, that being armor restriction, is already moot if you take Ebon Shadow since that MA is naked-only.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking of taking Silk Armor just for that reason and an Artifact Tiger Claw. TBH I'm not sure which is more important because Artifact Weapons don't make Decisives better and the Night Stealth Dodge ES build is basically an assassination style. I also don't know how likely it is that anyone is even going to hit me considering there's a battle group of Might 1 pirates, a god-tiger, a melee sorcerer, et al. <br /> <br /> Defense, offense, both? Im starting at E1. I'm designing my own tiger claws to fit my theme as well","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T11:25:23-08:00","id":1353061,"title":"","content":"Quite a few Artifacts have Evocations which enhance Decisives. Mela's Coil is armor that enhances a Decisive.<br /> <br /> I'd say weapon is way more important than armor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-06T12:25:22-08:00","id":1353092,"title":"","content":"Don't forget the Belt of Shadow Walking - +3 to all stealth rolls and transform into living shadow (to get into lots of hard to reach places)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1351803-crime-pays-larceny-stealth-and-ebon-shadow?p=1352934#post1352934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure which is more important because Artifact Weapons don't make Decisives better...</div> </div> </div> </div>Nani?<br /> <br /> <b>Vengeant (Black Jade Razor Claws, Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Breath-Denying Vengeance Current<br /> This is a gambit whose difficulty is (higher of target\u2019s Essence or Stamina). Success causes the victim to begin asphyxiating (Exalted, p. 232).<br /> <br /> Drink the Lesser Seas<br /> To use this Evocation, the wielder must be in concealment. She makes a decisive attack against an enemy who\u2019s unaware of her, adding (Essence) dice of damage and doubling 10s on the damage roll.<br /> <br /> <b>Frost-Thorn Knuckles (Moonsilver Razor Claws, Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> Glacial Beast Claw<br /> This Evocation enhances a decisive attack. A damaged enemy is knocked prone and covered with a layer of thick frost that imposes a \u22123 penalty on his rolls to rise from prone (Exalted, 198).<br /> <br /> Blood-Freezing Strike<br /> Blood-Freezing Strike is a decisive attack that can only be made against a prone enemy, adding (Strength) damage dice. Additionally, the victim loses 1 Initiative for each 10 on the decisive damage roll. The wielder doesn\u2019t gain this Initiative. An enemy crashed by this Initiative loss is frozen in place, unable to take any movement actions except to rise from prone until he recovers from crash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24362,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24362-fredo","user":"Fredo","date":". 12-06-2019, 03:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24362-fredo","name":"Fredo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-08T23:08:13-08:00","id":1353709,"title":"","content":"I took a<span style=\"font-family:arial\">ll the great advice</span> in this thread and made my first proper Ex3 character, a <b>Night Caste</b> names <i>Smiling Tiger</i> and had a Session 0 with my future ST.<br /> <br /> I started with<b> Ebon Shadow, Stealth, and Larceny</b> at 5. <b>Dodge, Athletics, Tiger Style</b> and some other stuff were at 3. I have the Artifact<b> Vengeant </b><div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</span></span></div>and <b>Belt of Shadow Walking</b> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf.</span></span></div> I didn't realize how much I was gonna miss those 10 committed motes, not going to lie. E1 is 13/33 so it's literally 20% of my essence pool to <span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">keep those things on. I also kept forgetting to add the +3 Stealth dice from the </span><b>Belt</b><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">, but its very useful. </span><br /> <br /> <b>Stalking Shadow Spirit</b><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"> from </span><i>Miracles</i><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"> is the coolest charm, I used it twice. It made me feel like I was really in control of the places I snuck in to, and i went from Resources 0 to Resources 2 by casing a Jeweler's and then using </span><b>SSS </b><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\">with </span><b>Flawless Pickpocket</b><span style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif\"> to steal a wide array of jewels and gold. </span><b>Living Shadow </b><b>Preparation</b> is another <i>incredible</i> charm. I have two separate pools of successes to use whenever I need them. <b>LSP</b> can be used anytime anywhere, but i have to use all of it at once. <b>SSS</b> can be rationed out as needed, but only in a single location that I've cased out. Both of these pools were 6 or 7 successes big. <br /> <br /> Larceny's <b>Seasoned Criminal Method</b> was also amazingly useful both for RP and for dealing with criminals. I looked like a desperate mark to one greedy jeweler, I looked like a sailor on shore leave ready to blow a months pay on dice booze and girls to the door guards of a teahouse crime front, and I convinced the inner guard that I was a prospective member to get access to the Big Boss. All from one charm with no mote cost. Its great. I have <b>Unshakable Rogue Spirit</b> but I didn't use it and I'm not sure if I like it. I don't think I need the extra success it offers but the idea of stealing from yourself is hysterical. <br /> <br /> <b>Graceful Crane Stance </b>and <b>Monkey Leap</b> were ok for some thematic stuff, Naruto roof hopping and stunts, but I didn't feel like I <i>needed</i> them. They unlock a lot of cool stuff though, so they'll stay.<br /> <br /> <b>Sensory Acuity Prana</b> helped a bit (double 9s on its own isn't great with a dicepool of 6) but I fell in love with the <b>Keen Sense</b> line of charms and I'm going to by all of them. Especially <b>Hearing and Touch</b>, but I don't have them yet. <br /> <br /> I bought <b>Reed in the Wind</b> but didn't need it yet, its there as a safety feature. It's my only defense charm besides the bonus from Ebon Shadow Style. I had only one fight in my Session 0 and it was me ambushing them to almost instant death. <br /> <br /> So, on to the fightin bits. <b>Vengeant</b> with the first Evocation unlocked (but unused), it's a weird ability where you slowly accumulate initiative against what I assume is supposed to be unaware targets. I didn't have a chance to use it yet. <br /> <br /> I have the first three charms of <b>Ebon Shadow</b>, and they were each useful. I have <b>Striking Fury Claw</b> as well. <br /> <br /> So I watched a Shikari try to shake down a Lost Egg Crime Lord for my location (we'd spoken earlier that night), and when words turned to blows I took action. I was already in Shadow Form from the <b>Belt</b> (holy <i>shit, </i>10 motes on top of 10 committed cuts deep), and I attacked from complete stealth. I used <b>Blinding Battle Feint</b> to roll JB and start in stealth, blew my <b>Living Shadow Prep </b>and <b>Stalking Shadow Spirit</b> pools to get a starting Initiative of <b>15</b> (to the delight of my ST, a current Single Point Stylist) to the Shikari's 6. Automatic Ebon Shadow Form (giving me even more Initiative, 18 to 5). <b>Seven Points of Weakness </b>and <b>Striking Fury Claw </b> made the attack <i><b>shockingly brutal</b></i> and I went from 18 Initiative to <b><u><i>FORTY TWO</i></u><i>, </i></b>the highest our game has ever reached. I crashed the shit of the Shikari and because of stunts put her head into a hotpot and left her windless and dazed. She spends her turn just standing up and trying to get a read on where I am. <br /> <br /> So I<b> Decisived</b> for 42 dice and did 14 damage. Instantly dead. <br /> <br /> I did a little RP stuff from there and it was all great. Smiling Tiger is now headed to the Main Plot on a ship owned by one of the PCs. <br /> <br /> He left the body of the Shikari (sans white jade armor) in a dingy pushed out of port with a letter in the boat that simply says &quot;The Dragon Eater Ate Well&quot; (my crime alias is the Dragon Eater, a killer who takes down Dynasts who deal in the criminal world). <br /> <br /> I had a lot of fun. I went through motes a lot quicker than I thought I would. 15 charms is a thin budget when youre the one making characters, I only took one charm in my supernal ability that wasn't E1, and there's always another 10 charms you want to complete your build. You have to make big sacrifices in Abilities to get what you want from the start too.<br /> <br /> I really felt like a character with a specific theme who had a niche carved for himself and I didn't feel like I spread myself too thin. <br /> <br /> I can't wait to start playing! Special thanks to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar531_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"531\" data-vbnamecard=\"531\">JohnDoe244</a> for the charm advice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T03:40:47-08:00","id":1353752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1351803-crime-pays-larceny-stealth-and-ebon-shadow?p=1353709#post1353709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't realize how much I was gonna miss those 10 committed motes, not going to lie.</div> </div> </div> </div>The price of being awesome.<br /> <br /> (That said, attuning to an artifact doesn\u2019t take twenty minutes like it did in 2e anymore, so if you\u2019re willing to let it be heavy and cumbersome when you\u2019re not using it, you could drop the commitment to the artifact weapon when you\u2019re not using it.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1351803-crime-pays-larceny-stealth-and-ebon-shadow?p=1353709#post1353709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Larceny's <b>Seasoned Criminal Method</b> was also amazingly useful both for RP and for dealing with criminals. I looked like a desperate mark to one greedy jeweler, I looked like a sailor on shore leave ready to blow a months pay on dice booze and girls to the door guards of a teahouse crime front, and I convinced the inner guard that I was a prospective member to get access to the Big Boss. All from one charm with no mote cost. Its great.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, for sure. I took it on my Knight Raiton character and have never regretted it. As a reminder, there\u2019s also a mien you can adopt that makes it harder to be investigated; I get a feeling you might need it after some of the stuff you\u2019ve done. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1351803-crime-pays-larceny-stealth-and-ebon-shadow?p=1353709#post1353709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Graceful Crane Stance </b>and <b>Monkey Leap</b> were ok for some thematic stuff, Naruto roof hopping and stunts, but I didn't feel like I <i>needed</i> them. They unlock a lot of cool stuff though, so they'll stay.</div> </div> </div> </div>Make sure and get Thunderbolt Attack Prana for those times you attack <i>without</i> 42 Initiative. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1351803-crime-pays-larceny-stealth-and-ebon-shadow?p=1353709#post1353709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Sensory Acuity Prana</b> helped a bit (double 9s on its own isn't great with a dicepool of 6) but I fell in love with the <b>Keen Sense</b> line of charms and I'm going to by all of them. Especially <b>Hearing and Touch</b>, but I don't have them yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Make sure and remember that <b>Surprise Anticipation Method</b> can potentially make all the indefinite-awesome-senses Charms free.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1351803-crime-pays-larceny-stealth-and-ebon-shadow?p=1353709#post1353709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did a little RP stuff from there and it was all great. Smiling Tiger is now headed to the Main Plot on a ship owned by one of the PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a ton of fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T14:31:24-08:00","id":1353963,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a> i didnt even consider un-attuning. I'll make a note of that. Good thinking!<br /> <br /> I def want Thunderbolt Attack Prana and Surprise Anticipation Method. TAP especially makes assassin builds assassiny-er","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}